# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# WHY THE CSP IS LISTED PER PAGE INSTEAD OF ON /*
#
# A browser enforces EVERY Content-Security-Policy header it receives, taking
# the intersection. So a CSP on /* cannot be relaxed for a subpath: putting a
# looser policy on /walkthroughs/* just sends two headers and the stricter one
# still applies. Rule order makes no difference; this was tested.
#
# The walkthroughs are vendored knitr exports that load jQuery, Bootstrap and
# highlight.js from data: URIs. Permitting those would need `script-src data:`,
# which is an XSS vector and would gut the policy for the whole site. They are
# therefore left without a CSP, and the real pages are listed individually.
#
# Adding a new page means adding it here, or it ships with no CSP.

/
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-tHd4qJ0R/vQfI0CbRTiL3XGSi+Tun7VhOcDbx08aLKA=' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

